# Copy the values into the place your app reads its environment from
# (this workspace's .env, or your app platform's environment settings).
# Get the string from: Neon Console -> your project -> "Connect" button.
#
# SECURITY: paste secrets ONLY into your own environment settings, never into a chat.
# If a connection string ever leaked, reset the role password in Neon (Roles -> Reset password).

# Neon Postgres — pooled hostname (-pooler) is the default Neon gives you:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://MYUSER:MYPASSWORD@ep-XXXX-XXXX-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require

# Use the DIRECT (unpooled) string — same host WITHOUT "-pooler", port 5432 —
# only if your driver/tool needs a native TCP connection (e.g. pg_dump, some migrations):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://MYUSER:MYPASSWORD@ep-XXXX-XXXX.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require

# Re-add any other variables your app had (placeholders — fill with your real values):
# SESSION_SECRET=...
# GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=...
# GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=...
# GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN=...
# GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=...
